# Prisma +
{{pascal stack.database.provider}}

> Database patterns for
{{project.name}}
using Prisma with
{{stack.database.provider}}. ## When to Use Load this skill when working on database schema,
migrations, seeds, or any ORM queries. ## Schema Rules - Every model must have an `id` field (UUID
by default) - Every model must have `createdAt` and `updatedAt` timestamps - Use `@relation` for all
foreign keys with explicit names - Use enums for fixed-value fields - Add `@@index` for commonly
queried fields - Add `@@unique` for business-key combinations ## Migration Workflow 1. Edit
`schema.prisma` 2. Run `npx prisma migrate dev --name descriptive-name` 3. Verify migration SQL is
correct 4. Update seed file if new models added ## Query Patterns - Use `findUnique` for single
record by unique field - Use `findMany` with `where`, `orderBy`, `skip`, `take` for lists - Use
`include` for eager loading relations (max 2 levels deep) - Use transactions for multi-model writes:
`prisma.$transaction([...])` ## References - [schema-template](references/schema-template.md) -
[seed-template](references/seed-template.md)
